## Key Design Decisions

### 1. Unidirectional Data Flow
- L1 sensors feed into L2/L3/L4/L5 simultaneously
- Avoids circular dependencies and deadlocks
- L5 provides asymmetric feedback to L3 only for learning

### 2. Battery as Primary Metric
- Battery level is the universal decision criterion
- DVFS policy, C-state selection, leader election all respect battery
- Emergency mode activated at battery<5%, failover at battery<2%

### 3. Reuse Philosophy
- Every component built on proven Phase 6-9 designs
- Bayesian confidence update identical to Phase 6
- 5-state FSM copied from Phase 6 LearningStateMachine
- Thermal throttling logic from Phase 8
- Workload classification from Phase 9

### 4. Quantitative Validation
- All 8 rules have precise numeric thresholds
- No subjective assessments
- Metrics struct tracks all rule compliance in real-time
- all_rules_passed() returns boolean for automatic validation

